  "result": "Perfect! I've created `src/export.js` with CSV export functionality and comprehensive tests.\n\n**What was implemented:**\n- **`exportCsv(invoices)`** exports invoices as CSV with header `number,customer,issueDate,dueDate,status,subtotal,discount,vat,total,due`. Amounts are formatted as euros with 2 decimals and a dot (e.g., \"1234.50\") with no thousands separator. Customer names come from invoice customerId lookups. CSV escaping: fields with commas or double quotes are wrapped in quotes, and internal double quotes are escaped by doubling.\n- **23 tests** covering header line, single/multiple invoices, amount formatting, subtotal/discount/VAT/total/due calculations, partial payments, CSV escaping with commas and quotes, invoice order preservation, edge cases, and mutation checks\n\nAll 296 tests pass (the original 273 plus 23 new tests for exportCsv).",
